<title>USA: Pep Boys files $150 mln shelf of debt.</title>
<headline>Pep Boys files $150 mln shelf of debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pep Boys - Manny, Moe &amp; Jack, filed Monday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $150 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>The Philadelphia-based auto parts retailer said proceeds from the sale will be used for working capital needs, to repay outstanding debt or for other general corporate needs.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
